<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell Aug 1-5 lifting fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell Aug 1-5 lifting fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of 3.0-percent sulphur, 180-centistoke fuel oil for August 1-5 lifting, a CPC source said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on July 15 and bids will be valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last tender, Taiwan sold two 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil cargoes for first half July lifting at around $100.50 per tonne on a free-on-board Kaohsiung basis, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3093)</p>
